<tr>
<td>Supplemental Information</td>
<td><div>Standard data file formats and codes used in those formats may be represented in two ways in this archival information package. A full list of all formats are in a file called NODC_Standard_Formats.txt and a list of codes used in those standard formats are in a file called NODC_Numeric_Codes.txt.<br><br>Many, but not all standard formats for which there is a 'C' or 'F' identifier, have a separate file containing only the data file format description and any codes specifically used in that format, using the filename convention Cnnn_Format_Code.txt or Fnnn_Format_Code.txt (where 'Cnnn' or 'Fnnn' is the file format identifier as described in the Abstract). Some standard data file formats use no specific codes, so the filename convention for those data file formats is Cnnn_Format.txt or Fnnn_Format.txt.<br><br>Some standard data file formats used a name rather than a 'C' or 'F' as the primary means of identifying those formats, e.g. Station Data 2 (SD2), Universal BathyThermograph (UBT), so the commonly-used name is used as the filename convention for those format description files.</div></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="col-md-3">Purpose</td>
<td>This dataset is available to the public for a wide variety of uses including scientific research and analysis.</td>
</tr>
